# W4-UI-2 C4: a click on the construction menu's public category, cell (0, 0) (data/ui/
# construction.txt's grid click centre (833, 330); type 501, the pioneer house) arms that type
# through ConstructionMenu/DevTool::arm - not the developer tool's own Next/PrevType cycle - then
# a click at the exact tile settlement_activity.script already proves free and buildable for this
# same type on lan5's developer island places it through the ordinary DevTool command path.
# Launch (viewer_wiring.py's own --app-arg list for this case):
#   --play data/maps/lan5.txt --construction-menu on --layout data/ui
# The window's default drawable is 1280 x 800 (viewer.cpp's SDL_CreateWindow), not data/ui/'s
# 1024 x 768 reference; construction_handle only resolves clicks at that exact size (R3 is still
# open), so this script resizes first. `key b` opens the menu itself (data/ui/construction.txt's
# own `open_key B`) - a real collision with the developer tool's own B-toggle, resolved by state
# (construction_handle claims B only while the menu is not yet open).
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
key b
wait frames 5
click_px 833 330
wait frames 5
expect title build 501
click 1156 516
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
# ESC is the menu's own key while it is open (data/ui/construction.txt's `leave_key ESC`): it
# closes the menu, not the window (the window's own Esc-quits-the-app binding would end the
# session here, which `quit` below would then never reach - proving the collision resolves to
# the menu, not the window, is the point of this step).
key esc
wait frames 5
# The menu is closed now: the same grid pixel does nothing (falls through; no further command).
click_px 833 330
wait frames 5
quit
